Alembic single-database migration environment for Gluevenir's CockroachDB schema.

Run migrations with `DATABASE_URL` set in the environment:

    uv run alembic upgrade head

The connection string is never stored in repository configuration.

CockroachDB reports this environment as non-transactional DDL. Before the first
upgrade, run the read-only preflight and require a clean dedicated database:

    uv run python scripts/check_live_migration_state.py --expect clean

After a successful upgrade, require the current state:

    uv run python scripts/check_live_migration_state.py --expect current

If a non-transactional pre-release migration fails before Alembic records its
target revision, do not rerun it over partial objects and do not add
`IF NOT EXISTS`. Preserve the error for diagnosis. `gluevenir_app` is
cluster-scoped, so recreating only the database does not remove a partially
created role. During this pre-release synthetic-only phase, first confirm the
exact dedicated database and inspect the exact role's memberships. Revoke only
confirmed Gluevenir runtime memberships, drop only the dedicated synthetic
database so its policies and grants no longer reference the role, remove only
the now-unreferenced `gluevenir_app` role, recreate only the dedicated database,
and rerun the clean preflight. Never use broad role or database cleanup. Once
any non-synthetic or released environment exists, recover with a new forward
Alembic revision instead of recreating it.
